{
  "id": "api_gravity__definition__calculation__and_converte",
  "title": "API Gravity: Definition, Calculation, and Converter",
  "description": "API expresses the gravity or density of liquid petroleum products. Convert between API Gravity and Specific Gravity using standard formulas.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# API Gravity: Definition, Calculation, and Converter\n\nAPI expresses the gravity or density of liquid petroleum products. It is devised jointly by the American Petroleum Institute and NIST.\n\n## Formulas\n\n**API Gravity from Specific Gravity:**\n\n°API = (141.5 / SG) - 131.5\n\n**Specific Gravity from API Gravity:**\n\nSG = 141.5 / (°API + 131.5)\n\nWhere:\n- °API = Degrees API Gravity\n- SG = Specific Gravity (at 60°F)\n\n**Note:** Oil with the least specific gravity has the highest API gravity. Density is temperature-dependent; the standard measuring temperature is 15°C or 60°F."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "sg_input",
          "label": "Specific Gravity (SG)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.85,
          "unit": "-"
        },
        {
          "id": "api_input",
          "label": "API Gravity (°API)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 30,
          "unit": "°API"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "api_from_sg",
          "label": "API Gravity from SG",
          "formula": "(141.5 / inputs.sg_input) - 131.5",
          "unit": "°API",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "sg_from_api",
          "label": "Specific Gravity from API",
          "formula": "141.5 / (inputs.api_input + 131.5)",
          "unit": "-",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
